If you stand in the doorway, you can usually see at least 2 squares
into a corridor.  If you can see two squares, it's (almost) never a
closet.
If you only see one square on the other side, it might be a closet.

It doesn't apply to non-secret doors, but some roles start with
'automatic searching' that will detect secret doors without you
expressly (s)earching them out.


